  "passage": {
    "text": "How does an apple get from the farm to your table? First, the farmer harvests the apples in the orchard. Then a truck takes them to a large warehouse. There, a wholesaler sorts the apples and packs them in boxes. After that, other trucks deliver the boxes to supermarkets. Many people work in this supply chain, and each one wants a share of the money. So the retail price is much higher than the price the farmer gets. Some farmers sell directly to customers at a local market. Then they earn more.",
